# Cube8Mod36 (generated by gen_certificate.py; core Lean, no Mathlib, no `sorry`, no `native_decide`)

Claim certified: let F = {0, 6, 12, 30} as residues modulo 36 and, for any N divisible by 36,
A_N = { x < N : x mod 36 is not in F }. Then A_N contains no projective 8-cube: for EVERY list of
8 natural numbers some nonempty index subset has its Z_N sum outside A_N. Also |A_(36 k)| = 32 k.

Model (the same as in `../cube_kernel/BINDING.md`): an element of Z_N is a natural number and the group sum of
a family is its ordinary sum reduced modulo N; a multiset of size d is a list of length d; an index subset is
a Boolean mask, nonempty when some entry is true; the full index set is included; there is no base point.

Method: a memoised search over the sets of sub-sums reachable by sequences with no forbidden sub-sum.
The file lists, for each depth k < 8, every reachable set (`lv k`); the kernel checks that the lists are
closed under appending any residue (either a forbidden sub-sum appears, or the new set is in the next list)
and that no set survives to depth 8 (one `decide +kernel` per bucket, assembled into `chain_ok`). `sound` proves that such a closed
chain forces a forbidden sub-sum in every sequence of length 8. The lists are DATA produced by a Python
script; nothing about them is trusted: if a list were incomplete or wrong the closure check would fail, and
`sound` only uses the inclusion "every member of a listed set is a genuine sub-sum", which it proves.
Reachable sets per depth: depth 0: 1 sets; depth 1: 32 sets; depth 2: 448 sets; depth 3: 3191 sets; depth 4: 9136 sets; depth 5: 5247 sets; depth 6: 1301 sets; depth 7: 108 sets; depth 8: 0 sets.
